  s_cal: "Level-match devices (make equally loud)", t_cal: "To make levels of different devices comparable, all microphones measure the same steady sound at the same time. The gain is adjusted per device so that all selected devices show the same level – the average of their measurements. There is no reference device. Each measurement is recorded with time and values and appears in the noise log.", h_cal: "1. Tick the devices (at least two) and put them all side by side (same distance). 2. “Start measurement”: 5 s quiet. 3. At “Switch the sound on now” start a steady sound (extractor hood, hair dryer …) – or choose under “Test sound” where it is played, then it runs by itself. At least 10 dB louder than the quiet. 4. Apply the result. Then put the devices back in their rooms.", cal_devs: "Devices:", cal_secs: "Duration", cal_start: "Start measurement", cal_q: "Measuring quiet – please be silent … {s} s", cal_on: "Switch the sound on now! … {s} s", cal_meas: "Measuring … {s} s", cal_eval: "Evaluating …", cal_result: "Result – please check and apply:", cal_few: "At least two devices must be measurable. Make the sound louder and steadier and measure again.", cal_apply: "Apply and record", cal_check: "Only record (check)", cal_discard: "Discard", cal_note_ph: "Note, e.g. “noise from a phone, all on the dining table”", cal_th_quiet: "Quiet (dBFS)", cal_th_lvl: "Sound (dBFS)", cal_th_dev: "Deviation", cal_th_gain: "Gain", cal_bad_nodata: "no values (device offline?)", cal_bad_quiet: "too quiet (at least 10 dB above quiet)", cal_bad_unsteady: "not steady", cal_done_apply: "✓ Applied and recorded.", cal_done_check: "✓ Recorded (gain unchanged).", cal_log_head: "Previous level matchings", cal_kind_apply: "applied", cal_kind_check: "checked", cal_ok_at: "✓ level-matched {d}", cal_changed: "⚠ gain changed since level matching", cal_none: "not level-matched", cal_target: "Target is the average of the selected devices: {v} dBFS.",
